WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:05.480
<b>Near Bolton, Deserted Pioneer Town, One Year Ago</b>

00:10.460 --> 00:13.320
Máni! We're leaving!

00:14.650 --> 00:15.570
Yes.

00:16.450 --> 00:18.900
Suddenly telling us all 
to abandon the village...

00:19.350 --> 00:21.920
It's not like we have anywhere else to go.

00:22.250 --> 00:25.450
Those nobles doing whatever they pleased

00:25.450 --> 00:28.200
is why the village's economy 
tanked in the first place.

00:28.200 --> 00:30.940
And once things were well beyond saving,

00:30.940 --> 00:35.670
they just gave up on the village and 
fled to the neighboring country.

00:35.670 --> 00:39.310
I'm never trusting nobles 
ever again after this.

00:39.310 --> 00:42.380
They just forced all the hardships onto us.

00:42.720 --> 00:47.100
Even your own husband worked 
himself until he fell ill,

00:47.100 --> 00:52.840
and they wouldn't give him proper treatment. 
Those stupid nobles practically killed him.

00:54.880 --> 01:00.020
<i>What was I even born for?</i>

02:32.500 --> 02:37.510
<b>Episode 10
Takumi Takes on Pioneering!</b>

02:32.500 --> 02:37.510
<b>Episode 10
Takumi Takes on Pioneering!</b>

02:33.120 --> 02:35.460
Over 1,000 citizens
driven out of their village

02:35.460 --> 02:41.960
have been graciously accepted
by Count Rockford.

02:38.510 --> 02:41.510
<b>One Year After Abandoning the Village</b>

02:42.510 --> 02:45.530
Those irredeemable nobles,

02:45.530 --> 02:47.370
abandoning their people like that.

02:47.950 --> 02:49.900
It's no use getting angry now.

02:50.250 --> 02:53.850
We can't abandon those 
who have lost their homes.

02:54.340 --> 02:56.840
It's been a year since he 
accepted the refugees.

02:57.210 --> 02:58.940
Count Rockford has sent us a missive

02:58.940 --> 03:03.320
requesting that we secure 
a new home for the refugees.

03:03.610 --> 03:08.400
With over 1,000 of them, 
we'll need a fair amount of land.

03:08.400 --> 03:09.790
But that means...

03:10.790 --> 03:12.750
This place is the only option.

03:13.130 --> 03:15.460
Yes. Though that's...

03:15.790 --> 03:18.850
a land where monsters run rampant.

03:18.850 --> 03:21.430
It won't be easy to develop.

03:21.790 --> 03:22.850
There's no choice.

03:22.850 --> 03:27.390
<i>He's</i> the only one capable of 
overcoming this dilemma.

03:27.970 --> 03:31.110
I think we should try challenging a dungeon!

03:37.020 --> 03:40.730
<i>I've been wanting to try challenging 
a dungeon for a while.</i>

03:41.420 --> 03:43.540
<i>So out of the many dungeons available,</i>

03:43.540 --> 03:46.950
<i>we set foot into the A-Rank Dungeon 
listed as the second most difficult:</i>

03:46.950 --> 03:49.390
<i>the Forest of the Beast King.</i>

03:50.180 --> 03:54.180
<i>It was a mysterious space with vast skies 
and woods, despite being underground.</i>

03:55.360 --> 03:57.630
<i>The monsters that appeared in the dungeon</i>

03:57.630 --> 04:00.910
<i>were overwhelmingly stronger than those 
outside, and there were a lot of them.</i>

04:02.390 --> 04:05.310
<i>However, even with the
 trees hindering visibility,</i>

04:05.310 --> 04:08.340
<i>Maple detected the monsters 
well before they could approach.</i>

04:10.960 --> 04:14.880
<i>Since we had Titan to take 
all of the monsters' attacks,</i>

04:16.180 --> 04:19.590
<i>we were able to defeat the bosses 
of each floor one after another,</i>

04:20.310 --> 04:23.290
<i>and obtain the treasures and items 
that lay within the treasure chests.</i>

04:25.610 --> 04:29.840
<i>After a whole day,
 we reached the last floor.</i>

04:30.450 --> 04:35.300
So, this path leads to the last boss, right?

04:35.660 --> 04:37.500
I'm excited!

04:37.500 --> 04:39.120
Come on out, last boss!

04:39.120 --> 04:42.320
We managed to make it this far 
without taking any major damage.

04:42.320 --> 04:43.050
Yeah.

04:43.050 --> 04:45.100
It was easy since there 
weren't any real traps.

04:47.060 --> 04:47.740
Huh?

04:47.740 --> 04:49.000
A click?

04:49.000 --> 04:50.860
Don't tell me...

04:52.690 --> 04:54.400
No way!

04:54.400 --> 04:56.950
Everyone, retreat!

04:56.950 --> 04:58.460
What a huge ball!

04:58.460 --> 05:00.970
You think this is some kind 
of carnival, don't you?

05:00.970 --> 05:04.100
It's life or death for me!

05:06.370 --> 05:10.360
Hey, wouldn't Titan have been 
able to break that iron ball?

05:10.740 --> 05:14.270
Since I shouted 
"Everyone, retreat!" right away,

05:14.270 --> 05:16.830
Titan followed that command to the letter.

05:17.120 --> 05:19.880
<i>Master's orders are absolute!</i>

05:19.880 --> 05:22.210
It's an exemplary pet.

05:24.110 --> 05:26.950
We'll just have to advance 
down this passage.

05:35.370 --> 05:38.510
Do you think we've been... lured here?

05:39.040 --> 05:40.790
Master. It's here.

05:40.790 --> 05:41.190
Huh?

05:42.270 --> 05:43.160
Here it comes!

05:48.570 --> 05:50.000
<i>The last boss?!</i>

05:52.820 --> 05:54.390
It's huge!

05:54.390 --> 05:55.740
An Earth Dragon.

05:55.740 --> 05:57.180
It's S-Rank.

05:57.700 --> 06:01.460
I should have brought Great Titan with us.

06:01.460 --> 06:03.920
<i>Master, it's not a problem.</i>

06:04.250 --> 06:05.870
Fan out!

06:07.880 --> 06:11.400
We won't get a chance
 to attack at this rate!

06:11.400 --> 06:13.150
Maple! Titan!

06:13.150 --> 06:14.870
Stop its tail from moving!

06:14.870 --> 06:15.800
Even a second will do!

06:16.050 --> 06:17.650
<i>Roger!</i>

06:27.240 --> 06:28.750
Wind Cutter!

06:30.080 --> 06:31.970
Foxfire Barrage!

06:32.550 --> 06:34.240
Fire Lance!

06:36.950 --> 06:37.940
Titan!

06:37.940 --> 06:39.400
Light of Judgment!

06:39.660 --> 06:41.330
<i>Light of Judgment.</i>

06:45.080 --> 06:46.760
We did it!

06:46.760 --> 06:47.770
Not yet!

06:51.920 --> 06:53.670
<i>Master!</i>

06:54.220 --> 06:55.680
Titan!

06:56.010 --> 07:00.100
Mr. Takumi, its weak point is its flank!

07:00.100 --> 07:01.060
Got it!

07:01.060 --> 07:02.130
Camellia!

07:05.010 --> 07:06.450
Here we go!

07:22.580 --> 07:24.790
We... did it?

07:24.790 --> 07:27.050
We did it, Mr. Takumi.

07:28.940 --> 07:30.550
<i>Good work.</i>

07:30.550 --> 07:32.720
We got the treasure chest!

07:32.720 --> 07:34.900
We conquered the dungeon!

07:34.900 --> 07:36.890
Huh? Over already?

07:42.230 --> 07:44.310
<b>Name</b>

07:42.230 --> 07:44.310
<b>Race</b>

07:42.230 --> 07:44.310
<b>Dragon Horse</b>

07:42.230 --> 07:44.310
<b>Camellia</b>

07:42.230 --> 07:44.310
<b>Takumi Iruma's Pet</b>

07:44.640 --> 07:47.420
Oh, Camellia's evolved into a Dragon Horse.

07:50.810 --> 07:52.650
Hm, look at this.

07:52.650 --> 07:55.390
I might be able to make 
something from this dragon part!

07:55.390 --> 07:59.420
Mr. Takumi, you really 
are a producer at heart.

07:59.420 --> 08:00.200
Huh?

08:01.300 --> 08:02.800
Yeah...

08:03.930 --> 08:06.510
<i>Shortly after we returned 
home from the dungeon,</i>

08:06.510 --> 08:09.790
<i>I was summoned by Marquis Godwin.</i>

08:10.090 --> 08:15.600
Mr. Iruma, are you aware of the undeveloped 
land in the southern region of my domain?

08:15.600 --> 08:16.760
Yes.

08:16.760 --> 08:20.150
Not only is it an uninhabited wilderness,
 but I hear there are so many monsters

08:20.150 --> 08:23.290
that even our neighboring 
nations completely ignore it.

08:24.010 --> 08:27.460
It was previously invaded 
by the Kingdom of Triaria,

08:27.460 --> 08:31.870
but their invasion failed, and it's said 
that failure led to their decline.

08:31.870 --> 08:34.990
But they also say that region

08:34.990 --> 08:39.750
is full of untapped adamantite 
and mythril ore veins, right?

08:40.270 --> 08:42.410
Does that mean you're interested?

08:42.690 --> 08:45.380
Well, not significantly—

08:44.500 --> 08:46.920
There's something I'd like to 
discuss with you, Mr. Iruma.

08:47.320 --> 08:48.370
Discuss?

08:48.370 --> 08:52.540
Would you be willing to build a 
pioneer village in that land?

08:52.900 --> 08:53.800
Huh?

08:56.440 --> 08:57.980
Why me?

08:57.980 --> 09:01.430
Mr. Iruma, I've heard about Bord Village.

09:01.730 --> 09:05.590
They tell me that you managed to create a 
sturdy wall around the village in a short time.

09:05.590 --> 09:06.680
Oh...

09:06.680 --> 09:10.850
So I'm asking this of you, 
because I think you can do it.

09:10.850 --> 09:15.700
Roughly 100 kilometers south of Bolton, 
there's a river and a spring.

09:15.700 --> 09:19.150
I think it would be best to start building 
the village around that water source.

09:19.430 --> 09:22.250
It's some distance away from 
the monsters' habitat as well.

09:22.250 --> 09:23.120
Please hold on.

09:23.700 --> 09:27.360
Lord, you're already aware of the situation 
currently surrounding Mr. Takumi—

09:27.360 --> 09:32.830
It does pain me to ask this of
Mr. Iruma when he's under threat.

09:32.830 --> 09:37.330
So you're saying that you're making 
this request in spite of that?

09:37.770 --> 09:38.740
Sofia.

09:39.290 --> 09:40.700
Please pardon me.

09:41.190 --> 09:43.210
You have a reason, don't you?

09:43.210 --> 09:45.560
A reason you need it developed quickly.

09:45.560 --> 09:46.250
Yes.

09:46.650 --> 09:50.030
There was a pioneer village that 
was deserted over a year ago.

09:50.740 --> 09:55.230
Development was halted due 
interference by corrupt nobles,

09:55.230 --> 09:58.750
but the villagers lost their 
homes and became refugees.

09:58.750 --> 10:01.940
We've been caring for them 
in Bolton and Rockford.

10:02.370 --> 10:03.390
Refugees?

10:03.390 --> 10:07.170
I want to build a home for 
them as quickly as possible.

10:07.170 --> 10:09.870
That's one of my reasons.

10:10.210 --> 10:11.780
There are other reasons?

10:12.240 --> 10:14.980
Very well. I accept.

10:14.980 --> 10:16.590
Mr. Takumi!

10:16.910 --> 10:21.550
I can't just ignore people 
who have lost their homes.

10:22.270 --> 10:24.080
You'll accept, then?

10:24.080 --> 10:25.270
I'm grateful!

10:25.270 --> 10:27.050
Well, you know...

10:27.670 --> 10:30.930
When I found myself without 
a home one year ago,

10:31.480 --> 10:34.800
there were people who welcomed me 
into their community with open arms.

10:36.420 --> 10:38.770
So I want to repay the favor.

10:41.470 --> 10:44.380
<i>I turned down the offer to have 
an escort of knights protect us,</i>

10:44.380 --> 10:48.060
<i>and the Wings of Nolyn set out 
for the frontier on our own.</i>

10:48.730 --> 10:52.070
<i>Sofia and the others agreed it 
would make things easier that way.</i>

10:53.040 --> 10:57.020
<i>Water was abundant and the environment 
was favorable in the frontier.</i>

10:58.110 --> 11:01.270
<i>We created ramparts with earth magic,</i>

11:02.890 --> 11:05.350
<i>dug deep moats along the outer perimeter,</i>

11:07.080 --> 11:09.010
<i>and constructed a strong fortress.</i>

11:16.210 --> 11:18.320
<i>The tasks of developing roads inside,</i>

11:19.620 --> 11:21.070
<i>building the aqueducts,</i>

11:22.070 --> 11:23.900
<i>logging groves,</i>

11:26.170 --> 11:28.250
<i>and exterminating monsters</i>

11:28.600 --> 11:32.030
<i>were divvied up between us, letting us 
make good progress with development.</i>

11:34.830 --> 11:36.860
It has become quite well-developed.

11:36.860 --> 11:37.680
Yeah.

11:38.040 --> 11:44.790
Sofia, I'm sorry, but could you go to Bolton 
and request the transfer of the pioneers?

11:44.790 --> 11:46.140
Very well.

11:49.760 --> 11:50.550
What?!

11:50.960 --> 11:55.780
He's ready to receive the citizens 
after just ten days of development?

11:56.050 --> 11:56.960
Yes.

11:56.960 --> 12:02.350
Mr. Takumi said they should be able to 
live their daily lives without issue.

12:04.110 --> 12:07.200
I heard we're going to the 
southern frontier this time.

12:07.470 --> 12:11.420
That's supposed to be the 
undeveloped land full of monsters.

12:11.420 --> 12:15.670
Reckon that means they're 
sending us to settle land

12:15.670 --> 12:17.890
near monsters to get rid of us.

12:18.150 --> 12:22.340
I've heard the village's operations are going
 to be run a man dispatched from Bolton.

12:22.340 --> 12:27.350
Probably just another noble who 
sees us all as disposable pawns.

12:27.350 --> 12:29.850
We're going back to that awful life.

12:31.460 --> 12:35.300
I guess a peaceful life is 
just too much for us to ask.

12:42.150 --> 12:45.210
Hey! Those are ramparts, aren't they?

12:49.640 --> 12:53.870
Welcome! You all must be
 worn out from your long trip.

12:54.460 --> 12:59.000
I was just working on preparing 
the land over there for farming.

12:59.000 --> 13:02.480
Wh-What is the meaning of this, Mr. Iruma?!

13:02.480 --> 13:06.820
Uh, I surrounded the village with ramparts 
to protect against monster attacks,

13:06.820 --> 13:08.910
then I dug a moat around it.

13:09.340 --> 13:13.150
It should be safe unless we're 
attacked by a dragon or something.

13:13.530 --> 13:15.540
That's not what I mean.

13:15.540 --> 13:17.990
Oh, you mean that fort?

13:17.990 --> 13:20.810
I built it for those in charge of governing.

13:21.460 --> 13:24.180
There are homes for everyone 
moving here to live in,

13:24.180 --> 13:26.840
and there's a barracks 
for the knights as well.

13:26.840 --> 13:30.780
The sewage is handled with a
 septic tank and magical devices.

13:31.410 --> 13:33.400
I'm grateful for your attention to detail.

13:33.400 --> 13:35.080
Wait, no!

13:35.080 --> 13:36.750
How did you build this
in such a short time?!

13:36.990 --> 13:38.940
I mean, this isn't even a village anymore!

13:38.940 --> 13:40.880
You've erected an entire fortress!

13:40.880 --> 13:43.390
No way. It's far from finished.

13:43.390 --> 13:45.020
No, this is definitely absurd!

13:45.020 --> 13:46.750
Is this some kind of magic?!

13:46.750 --> 13:49.210
Oh, yes. I did use magic.

13:49.470 --> 13:53.330
We really get to live here?

13:53.330 --> 13:55.020
This is incredible!

13:55.860 --> 13:57.580
Are you all alone?

14:00.840 --> 14:01.770
Yes.

14:01.770 --> 14:04.350
My husband passed away in our old village.

14:04.350 --> 14:09.090
I imagine it might be difficult 
to tend a farm all by yourself.

14:09.090 --> 14:10.630
No, not particularly.

14:11.400 --> 14:13.780
Do you have any interest 
in doing different work?

14:16.030 --> 14:18.970
I'll try consulting with my master.

14:18.970 --> 14:20.460
Your master?

14:20.460 --> 14:21.460
Who is he?

14:21.900 --> 14:24.670
The man who built this village.

14:24.670 --> 14:27.800
Right now, everyone's so 
busy developing the land,

14:27.800 --> 14:33.080
so I was thinking my master might need 
someone to help take care of him.

14:33.990 --> 14:36.830
Take care of... him?

14:36.830 --> 14:38.870
Can you cook?

14:38.870 --> 14:41.280
Yes, I can.

14:41.280 --> 14:42.910
Then there shouldn't be a problem.

14:44.640 --> 14:48.330
Why don't you try meeting with my master?

14:48.940 --> 14:50.530
I'll come collect you later.

14:55.440 --> 14:57.910
I heard the story from Sofia.

14:58.560 --> 15:00.540
Your name is Máni, right?

15:01.010 --> 15:01.920
Yes.

15:02.510 --> 15:04.440
As long as you're okay with it,

15:04.440 --> 15:07.720
then I'd love to ask for you 
to help take care of us.

15:07.960 --> 15:11.210
I'll pay you whatever wage 
we negotiate later as well.

15:12.500 --> 15:15.630
I'm never trusting nobles 
ever again after this.

15:15.630 --> 15:20.150
Even your own husband worked 
himself until he fell ill...

15:20.970 --> 15:22.660
My apologies.

15:22.660 --> 15:24.740
I'm afraid I can't accept.

15:24.740 --> 15:26.600
Wh-Why not?!

15:26.910 --> 15:30.820
I'm sorry. I... I...

15:30.820 --> 15:36.490
Will we have to face despair once 
more now that we're in this village?

15:37.070 --> 15:39.760
What did we even come here for?

15:39.760 --> 15:40.890
I...

15:41.270 --> 15:43.750
I just can't trust you.

15:44.070 --> 15:46.060
Mr. Takumi's not like that.

15:46.060 --> 15:47.450
Maria, it's okay.

15:47.870 --> 15:51.680
Then let's just shelve this offer for now.

15:57.170 --> 15:59.350
<i>After saying something like that to him...</i>

15:59.350 --> 16:01.060
<i>I can't stay here anymore.</i>

16:01.340 --> 16:04.060
<i>I'm sure he has eyes on me.</i>

16:04.060 --> 16:05.520
<i>I can't stay here.</i>

16:06.000 --> 16:10.750
<i>I know there's no guarantee that 
he'll be like the previous nobles...</i>

16:11.540 --> 16:13.760
<i>So why did I say such a thing?</i>

16:13.760 --> 16:15.030
<i>A sense of righteousness?</i>

16:15.750 --> 16:16.510
<i>No.</i>

16:17.100 --> 16:18.480
<i>I was lashing out.</i>

16:18.910 --> 16:23.450
<i>I was just venting my own frustration 
at being unable to do anything.</i>

16:42.030 --> 16:43.180
Master!

16:43.180 --> 16:45.850
Monsters are here! Lots of 'em!

16:46.420 --> 16:48.050
Monsters are here?!

16:48.050 --> 16:51.010
Yeah, the knights are 
in an uproar right now!

16:51.010 --> 16:52.760
See what I said!

16:52.760 --> 16:55.610
I'm sure they're going to send 
us out to dispatch the monsters!

16:56.150 --> 16:57.590
What's <i>that?!</i>

16:57.590 --> 16:58.630
A monster?!

16:58.630 --> 16:59.630
It's a golem!

17:00.520 --> 17:01.570
Mr. Iruma!

17:01.810 --> 17:05.230
Raise all the drawbridges 
and seal off the village.

17:05.230 --> 17:09.020
Dorn, please have your knights 
secure the safety of the villagers.

17:09.020 --> 17:09.790
But!

17:10.150 --> 17:13.880
There aren't any monsters who 
can get over these ramparts.

17:14.370 --> 17:16.350
We'll handle the monsters outside.

17:25.790 --> 17:28.850
I haven't been able to find Máni anywhere!

17:29.090 --> 17:33.570
Now that you mention it, I saw her 
head past the south drawbridge.

17:33.800 --> 17:35.890
Is she outside the ramparts?!

17:35.890 --> 17:37.030
Mr. Iruma!

17:37.860 --> 17:43.500
We won't let them harm even a 
single one of the villagers!

17:54.260 --> 17:57.460
<i>What was I...</i>

17:57.960 --> 18:00.170
<i>Oh. I see.</i>

18:00.660 --> 18:05.270
<i>So I was born to die here.</i>

18:05.270 --> 18:06.640
<i>That's all.</i>

18:09.790 --> 18:11.310
You're safe now.

18:14.520 --> 18:16.750
There are a lot more coming!

18:17.110 --> 18:19.950
I don't think they're going to be a problem.

18:20.190 --> 18:20.930
Huh?

18:21.310 --> 18:22.410
Mr. Takumi!

18:23.180 --> 18:25.380
I've exterminated all the monsters!

18:25.380 --> 18:27.380
They were no problem at all!

18:27.380 --> 18:28.870
Indeed!

18:28.870 --> 18:31.820
They were hardly worth fighting!

18:31.820 --> 18:33.460
<i>Good work.</i>

18:34.150 --> 18:35.120
See?

18:35.120 --> 18:37.090
Because we're the best party.

18:38.320 --> 18:39.810
You're hurt!

18:39.810 --> 18:43.840
Yeah, that Bush Wolf 
grazed me with its claws.

18:43.840 --> 18:45.000
I'm fine.

18:47.350 --> 18:48.410
Thank you.

18:50.120 --> 18:52.520
You got hurt for me.

18:52.520 --> 18:53.400
I'm sorry—

18:53.400 --> 18:55.690
I'm just glad that you weren't injured.

18:56.380 --> 19:00.180
I won't let anyone hurt the 
villagers living here.

19:00.570 --> 19:03.070
I want you all to live peaceful lives.

19:03.370 --> 19:04.530
<i>No.</i>

19:04.950 --> 19:06.260
<i>This man...</i>

19:06.750 --> 19:10.830
<i>He isn't anything like any of 
the nobles I've known so far.</i>

19:11.470 --> 19:14.680
<i>He's generous and kind.</i>

19:15.350 --> 19:16.340
Um...

19:16.340 --> 19:17.040
Yes?

19:17.590 --> 19:19.130
I know it's a bit late,

19:19.620 --> 19:24.750
but is that offer to be 
your maid still valid?

19:25.770 --> 19:26.810
Of course.

19:31.090 --> 19:33.180
You're hired.

19:33.180 --> 19:35.150
We're happy to have you!

19:35.150 --> 19:37.150
Welcome! To the Wings of Nolyn!

19:41.010 --> 19:42.950
Thank you for having me!

19:43.890 --> 19:45.200
I see.

19:45.200 --> 19:47.200
Mr. Iruma does good work.

19:47.200 --> 19:47.990
Yes.

19:47.990 --> 19:50.870
So? What's your opinion on that village—

19:50.870 --> 19:51.840
no, town?

19:52.380 --> 19:54.340
Can it serve as a wedge?

19:55.250 --> 19:58.260
<b>Holy Empire of Sidonia</b>

19:55.260 --> 19:58.260
The missive from the 
Kingdom of Triaria reads:

19:58.550 --> 20:00.880
"All of a sudden, a fortress 
town with a sturdy castle"

20:00.880 --> 20:04.210
"has been erected in the undeveloped 
lands near the Kingdom of Barcula."

20:04.210 --> 20:06.870
A whole fortress all of a sudden?

20:06.870 --> 20:10.770
They report the knights stationed 
there were dispatched from Bolton.

20:10.770 --> 20:12.420
From Bolton?

20:12.420 --> 20:16.570
Perhaps that alchemist is involved.

20:16.570 --> 20:18.020
Quite possible.

20:18.020 --> 20:22.570
One could also view this as a 
roundabout check on our empire.

20:23.010 --> 20:24.660
Those loathsome...

20:25.210 --> 20:28.610
We won't let the Kingdom of Barcula 
have their way forever.

20:29.250 --> 20:33.630
The one to dominate this continent 
shall be our Holy Empire of Sidonia.

20:33.630 --> 20:36.580
Elizabeth, then you mean...

20:36.790 --> 20:39.540
Please rejoice, Father.

20:40.330 --> 20:42.240
The time is ripe.

20:43.800 --> 20:46.480
We'll be using this road for trade,

20:46.480 --> 20:49.400
so maybe I should widen it a bit more.

20:50.030 --> 20:52.950
Mr. Takumi! Everyone!

20:53.320 --> 20:55.620
I've brought your lunches.

20:56.480 --> 20:58.990
I made a lot!

21:01.290 --> 21:03.320
I'm starving!

21:23.300 --> 21:27.960
Master! I felt some unpleasant mana!

21:28.500 --> 21:31.710
I have a bad feeling about this.

21:32.100 --> 21:33.450
One year.

21:33.450 --> 21:34.220
Huh?

21:36.900 --> 21:38.550
The truth is...

21:38.550 --> 21:42.220
I messed with time when 
I sent you on your way.

21:42.220 --> 21:45.420
I sent you to one year before
 the summoning of the heroes.

21:46.240 --> 21:49.490
It's been exactly a year 
since I arrived.

21:49.940 --> 21:52.040
So they're finally here.
